# Modular Code Enforcement

## File Size

- **Soft limit**: 200 lines of code per file
- **Hard limit**: 400 lines -- split into modules if approaching
- **Exempt**: Prompt templates, generated files, test fixtures

## Module Boundaries

- Each module has a clear single responsibility
- index.ts exports only -- no business logic
- Shared code goes in a shared/ directory, not duplicated

## Naming

- Files: kebab-case (e.g., `user-service.ts`, not `UserService.ts`)
- Directories: kebab-case
- No catch-all names: utils.ts, helpers.ts, service.ts, common.ts
- Name files after what they contain, not what they do generically

## Imports

- Relative within module (`./sibling`)
- Barrel imports across modules (`from "../shared"`)
- No path aliases (@/ etc.) -- relative imports only
